# ============================================================
#  Timeline (design §3.2, §4.4). `history` entries are dated canon
#  (years before the player's first year, as negative numbers; the
#  first year is 0). `beat` entries are the in-run calendar of fixed
#  beats (yNmM; m1 = Harvestmoon); in phase 2b they drive the dated
#  `auto` events. Context for authors; not shown in the game.
# ============================================================

# ---------------- History ----------------

@timeline founding
date: -300
kind: history
text: The founders raise seven towers above the Mirror Lake as a seal over the Hollow Star, with one lock in each tower and a star-shaped key. The entry for the founding year in the Founders' Ledger is later cut out with a razor.

@timeline prudence_ashworth
date: -200
kind: history
text: Prudence Ashworth, a student, dies before she can deliver a letter to the baker's daughter in the village. Her ghost stays in the dormitories, rearranging socks.

@timeline seventh_tower_locked
date: -100
kind: history
text: The seventh tower is locked. Nobody living remembers why, and the faculty prefer it that way.

@timeline the_frozen_spring
date: -60
kind: history
text: The lake freezes one spring night. Three students go down to the boathouse; only two come back. Maud is one of them; Edmund is the one who doesn't return. His silver wand is never buried.

@timeline thorne_and_the_storm
date: -40
kind: history
text: Aldric Thorne duels a storm, loses badly, and spends a year learning why. The rumour says he won. A rival from those years still wants a rematch.

@timeline isolde_appointed
date: -20
kind: history
text: Isolde Marrow, once the student who set the observatory on fire twice, becomes headmistress. Her student portrait is hidden in a forgotten corridor.

@timeline ledger_founded
date: -20
kind: history
text: The Lumen Ledger prints its first issue. Nobody has interviewed the headmistress since she took office.

@timeline kael_arrives
date: y1m3
kind: beat
event: kael_arrives
text: Kael Dumont arrives mid-term from the North, with frost on the dining-hall floor behind him.

# ---------------- The year's fixed beats (today's calendar; re-paced in phase 3) ----------------

@timeline harvest_feast
date: y1m1
kind: beat
event: choose_elective
text: The year begins: electives are chosen and the Harvest Feast is held.

@timeline club_fair
date: y1m2
kind: beat
event: club_fair
text: The Club Fair, and Lantern Night over the lake.

@timeline lantern_night
date: y1m2
kind: beat
event: lantern_night
text: Lantern Night: lanterns released over the Mirror Lake, each carrying a wish.

@timeline job_board
date: y1m3
kind: beat
event: job_board
text: The Job Board fills with term-time work.

@timeline winter_trials
date: y1m4
kind: beat
event: winter_trials
text: The Winter Trials, the first exams of the year.

@timeline midwinter_ball
date: y1m5
kind: beat
event: midwinter_ball
text: The Midwinter Ball in the Great Hall.

@timeline spring_tournament
date: y1m8
kind: beat
event: spring_tournament
text: The Spring Tournament on the duelling green.

@timeline grand_examinations
date: y1m10
kind: beat
event: grand_exams
text: The Grand Examinations close the academic year.

@timeline summer_recess
date: y1m11
kind: beat
event: summer_plans
text: Summer recess: the towers empty.

@timeline starfall
date: y1m12
kind: beat
event: starfall
text: Starfall, when the meteor showers come and the whole academy sleeps on the lawns.

@timeline the_night
date: y3m9
kind: beat
event: hs_the_night
text: The night the lake freezes. Moves to year 4 in the v0.3 calendar.
